From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:54:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 108/108] arm64: dts: exynos7570: j4lte: reserve the firmware
 memory at 0x7e700000

The downstream device tree keeps 0x7e700000-0x7e7fffff away from the
kernel (/memreserve/ 0x7E700000 0x100000 in exynos7570-rmem.dtsi), but
this one handed it out as System RAM. Something outside Linux writes
there at run time: under a sustained eMMC read streamed over the USB
RNDIS gadget, OpenWrt oopsed in pfifo_fast_dequeue on a freed sk_buff
(PA 0x7e783000), and with slub_debug on the skbuff caches the same
stress reported "Poison overwritten" within about four minutes: 64
aligned bytes zeroed in a freed skbuff_head_cache object at PA
0x7e7c1400. Both are inside the unreserved megabyte.

Verified on the J4 (6.12, slub_debug still on): /proc/iomem lists
7e700000-7e7fffff as reserved, and eight 2.5 GiB passes of the same
stress (about 12 minutes) ran without a SLUB report, with identical
hashes every pass.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts
index 80c5e502a..7cc167094 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts
@@ -61,6 +61,17 @@ bootloader-scratch@7e280000 {
 			no-map;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Firmware memory the downstream DT keeps away from the kernel
+		 * (/memreserve/ 0x7e700000 0x100000 in exynos7570-rmem.dtsi).
+		 * Something outside Linux writes into it at run time: handed
+		 * out as RAM, freed sk_buffs there got 64-byte blocks zeroed.
+		 */
+		firmware@7e700000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x7e700000 0x100000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
 		framebuffer@67000000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0x67000000 (720 * 1280 * 4)>;
 			no-map;
